('127.104.d.2.D',4,'Admixtures in mortar are added to change properties such as:','["Sand color", "Set time or workability", "Brick size", "Color of the sky"]'::jsonb,1,'Admixtures modify performance.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.E',3,'The common mortar types are M, S, N, O, and:','["A", "B", "K", "Z"]'::jsonb,2,'ASTM mortar types.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.E',4,'Type S mortar is used for:','["Painting", "Decorative trim", "Chimney flues", "Structural or below-grade applications"]'::jsonb,3,'Type S has higher strength.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.F',3,'Plastic mortar should be workable and able to:','["Hold the weight of units", "Run like water", "Crumble", "Fall apart"]'::jsonb,0,'It should be cohesive.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.F',4,'Good water retention in plastic mortar keeps it from:','["Freezing in July", "Drying out too quickly on the block", "Growing", "Turning blue"]'::jsonb,1,'Retention helps bond.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.G',3,'Hardened mortar must have good:','["Taste", "Odor", "Bond strength", "Noise"]'::jsonb,2,'Bond holds units together.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.G',4,'Hardened mortar should also be:','["Soft", "Brittle", "Edible", "Durable against weather"]'::jsonb,3,'Durability matters.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.H',3,'A common mortar problem is mortar that is too wet, which can cause:','["Slumping and weak joints", "Stronger joints", "Faster curing", "No change"]'::jsonb,0,'Too much water weakens it.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.H',4,'If mortar begins to stiffen on the board, it can be:','["Mixed with cement", "Retempered with water within allowable time", "Frozen", "Dumped on the wall"]'::jsonb,1,'Retempering is allowed briefly.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.I',3,'Too much sand in a mix tends to make mortar:','["Perfect", "Colorful", "Harsh and weak", "Sticky and strong"]'::jsonb,2,'Proportions matter.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.I',4,'Poor-quality sand with clay or silt can cause:','["Stronger walls", "Brighter color", "Faster set", "Weak bond and cracking"]'::jsonb,3,'Contaminated sand harms mortar.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.J',3,'In hot, windy weather mortar tends to:','["Dry out too fast", "Never set", "Freeze", "Become sweet"]'::jsonb,0,'Evaporation is rapid.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.K',3,'Efflorescence is a:','["Mortar color", "White powdery deposit of salts on masonry", "Roof", "Type of brick"]'::jsonb,1,'Salts migrate to the surface.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.K',4,'Efflorescence is caused by water moving through masonry and carrying:','["Paint", "Sugar", "Soluble salts", "Oil"]'::jsonb,2,'Moisture brings salts out.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.J',4,'Tempering mortar with a little water is allowed to restore workability but not to:','["Add color", "Dry it faster", "Add sand", "Exceed the allowed water for the mix"]'::jsonb,3,'Excess water weakens.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.L',3,'Setting up for mortar work includes placing the mixer, materials, and:','["Water source", "Paint", "Furniture", "Pillow"]'::jsonb,0,'Organize the mixing area.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.L',4,'Leftover mortar should be disposed of:','["In the creek", "According to site and environmental rules", "On a neighbor''s lawn", "Down a storm drain"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper disposal protects waterways.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.M',3,'A clean mixing area helps to avoid:','["Work", "Profit", "Contamination and accidents", "Mortar"]'::jsonb,2,'Housekeeping prevents errors.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.M',4,'Washing a mixer''s drum at the end of the day prevents:','["Quick drying", "Rusting only", "Rain", "Hardened mortar buildup"]'::jsonb,3,'Clean tools last.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.N',3,'The mortar mixing area should be placed:','["Close to the work and on firm ground", "Under power lines", "On a slope", "Far away"]'::jsonb,0,'Efficient layout saves effort.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.N',4,'Sand piles at the mixing area should be kept:','["Dirty", "Clean and covered when possible", "Open to dogs", "Wet with oil"]'::jsonb,1,'Protect materials from contamination.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.O',3,'When mixing mortar in a power mixer, the dry ingredients are typically added:','["All at once without water", "After the mixer is off", "With part of the water first, then the rest", "Never"]'::jsonb,2,'Staged mixing prevents lumps.','original'),
('127.104.d.2.O',4,'Mortar in a power mixer is generally mixed for:','["10 seconds", "1 day", "1 hour", "About 3 to 5 minutes"]'::jsonb,3,'Standard mixing time ensures uniformity.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.A',3,'Concrete masonry units usually have:','["Hollow cores", "No shape", "Solid gold", "Wood fibers"]'::jsonb,0,'CMUs are hollow.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.A',4,'A standard 8-inch CMU has actual dimensions of about:','["4 x 4 x 4", "7 5/8 by 7 5/8 by 15 5/8 inches", "12 x 12 x 12", "8 x 8 x 8"]'::jsonb,1,'Actual size leaves room for joint.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.B',3,'Setting up a CMU wall starts with a:','["Door", "Window", "Dry layout of the first course", "Roof"]'::jsonb,2,'Layout checks fit.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.B',4,'In a running bond, vertical joints in each course are:','["Absent", "Aligned", "Random", "Offset by half a unit"]'::jsonb,3,'Staggering distributes loads.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.C',3,'Face shell mortar bedding for hollow block means mortar is applied to the:','["Outer shells of the block", "Top only", "Cores", "Inside only"]'::jsonb,0,'Face-shell bedding is typical.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.C',4,'Tooling mortar joints is done when mortar is:','["Fully wet", "Thumbprint hard", "Frozen", "Fully dry"]'::jsonb,1,'Timing affects finish.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.D',3,'CMU walls are cleaned after the mortar:','["Is wet", "Is not placed", "Has begun to set but is not fully hard", "Has frozen"]'::jsonb,2,'Clean when mortar is partially set.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.D',4,'A stiff brush is used to clean CMUs to remove:','["Paint", "Color", "Texture", "Mortar crumbs and residue"]'::jsonb,3,'Brushing cleans faces.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.E',3,'Brick is classified by grade, type, and:','["Size", "Weight of sand", "Brand of mortar", "Weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Brick has several classifications.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.E',4,'Face brick is used where:','["Below grade only", "Appearance matters", "Never seen", "Hidden walls"]'::jsonb,1,'Face brick is for exposed walls.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.F',3,'A dry run for brick laying means:','["Finishing", "Wetting the brick", "Placing brick without mortar to check layout", "Painting"]'::jsonb,2,'Dry bonding checks spacing.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.F',4,'The first course of brick is laid in a full mortar bed on the:','["Roof", "Window", "Door", "Foundation or footing"]'::jsonb,3,'The base course sets the line.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.G',3,'A mason ''buttering'' the end of a brick is:','["Applying mortar to the end before placing it", "Painting it", "Cutting it", "Cleaning it"]'::jsonb,0,'Buttering fills head joints.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.G',4,'A convex or V joint tooled in brick is made with a:','["Hammer", "Jointer", "Saw", "Plane"]'::jsonb,1,'Jointers compress mortar.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.H',3,'After tooling, excess mortar on brick faces is removed with a:','["Hammer", "Plane", "Brush or cloth", "Level"]'::jsonb,2,'Brushing cleans faces.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.H',4,'Acid cleaning of brick should be done with:','["No water", "Bare hands", "No ventilation", "Care and protective equipment"]'::jsonb,3,'Chemicals are hazards.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.I',3,'A brick set (wide chisel) and hammer are used to:','["Split a brick along a scored line", "Level a wall", "Mix mortar", "Cut a rule"]'::jsonb,0,'Chisels cut bricks.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.I',4,'When cutting with a chisel and hammer, always wear:','["Nothing", "Eye protection", "A hat only", "Sandals"]'::jsonb,1,'Chips fly.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.J',3,'A masonry hammer has one square head and a:','["Claw", "Level", "Chisel end", "Saw"]'::jsonb,2,'Used for trimming brick.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.J',4,'Light, quick taps with a masonry hammer around a scored line help to:','["Lay the brick", "Crush the brick", "Mix mortar", "Break the brick cleanly"]'::jsonb,3,'Scoring then tapping splits it.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.K',3,'A masonry saw cuts with a:','["Diamond blade", "Paper blade", "Wood blade", "Plastic blade"]'::jsonb,0,'Diamond blades cut masonry.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.K',4,'A masonry splitter works by:','["Melting it", "Applying pressure to split the unit along a line", "Painting it", "Burning it"]'::jsonb,1,'Splitters break units cleanly.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.L',3,'After cutting a unit, check that it:','["Is wet", "Is painted", "Fits the space and has clean edges", "Is lighter"]'::jsonb,2,'Verify fit.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_16_v1'
from (values
('127.104.d.3.L',4,'A cut brick placed in a wall should have its cut face:','["Painted", "Unprotected", "Outward always", "Hidden from view if possible"]'::jsonb,3,'Cuts are less attractive.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.M',3,'Masonry reinforcement such as joint reinforcement is placed in the:','["Mortar bed", "Door", "Roof", "Window"]'::jsonb,0,'Reinforcement strengthens walls.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.M',4,'Vertical rebar in CMU walls is placed in:','["Roofs", "Grouted cores", "Footings only", "Paint"]'::jsonb,1,'Cores hold rebar and grout.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.N',3,'Masonry accessories such as anchors and ties connect:','["Colors", "Rugs", "The masonry to other building parts", "Paintings"]'::jsonb,2,'Ties anchor masonry.','original'),
('127.104.d.3.N',4,'Weep holes in a masonry wall allow:','["Air in only", "Sound", "Light", "Moisture to drain out"]'::jsonb,3,'Weep holes release water.','original'),
('127.100.d.1.K',3,'A board falls from a scaffold and hits a worker below. This injury is classified as:','["Struck-by", "Electrocution", "Caught-in", "Slip hazard"]'::jsonb,0,'Impact from a moving object is struck-by.','original'),
('127.100.d.1.K',4,'Barricading the area under overhead work mainly prevents which hazard?','["Heat illness", "Falling-object strikes", "Chemical burns", "Noise exposure"]'::jsonb,1,'Keeping people clear stops struck-by injuries.','original'),
('127.100.d.5.G',3,'Which document gives the required quality of lumber and fasteners for a house?','["Lunch order", "Parking permit", "Written specifications", "Time sheet"]'::jsonb,2,'Specs state material requirements.','original'),
('127.100.d.5.G',4,'Written specifications are read together with the drawings because they give:','["Only names", "Only dates", "Only costs", "Details too long to put on the plans"]'::jsonb,3,'Specs and plans complement each other.','original'),
('127.100.d.6.F',3,'Installing bridging in a floor system makes the joists share loads and:','["Stay straight", "Glow", "Shrink", "Rust"]'::jsonb,0,'Bridging holds joists upright.','original'),
('127.100.d.6.F',4,'Which is a purpose of herringbone bridging?','["Holding shingles", "Transferring load between neighboring joists", "Sealing windows", "Supporting stairs"]'::jsonb,1,'Bridging spreads loads.','original'),
('127.100.d.6.I',3,'Which fastener is best for attaching a subfloor to joists to reduce squeaks?','["Wire ties", "Staples only", "Screws with construction adhesive", "Masking tape"]'::jsonb,2,'Screws and adhesive stop movement.','original'),
('127.100.d.6.I',4,'Fastener length for a 3/4-inch subfloor must be long enough to:','["Pierce the ceiling", "Reach the foundation", "Stay in the panel only", "Penetrate well into the joist"]'::jsonb,3,'Embedment gives holding power.','original')
